xnu 0407: switch the panel to its 120 Hz timing

The 0406 build proves the timer and the published refresh at 120 (ring:
`vsync avg 8332 us`) but the glass stays at 60: `intf ... fc` moves +60 a
second and `panel` changes on 59 of 120 ticks, while the renderer reaches
108 swaps during a drag and the extra presents are coalesced. The ABL left
the panel in its 60 Hz timing for the splash.

The live device tree carries the panel's three timings and the vendor
timing-switch command for the 120 one (`timing@2`: 0x2f 0x00, 0x8b 0x00,
0xdf 0x20 and 0xce 0x01 around the two 0xf0 page writes). Send that
sequence once, after the first brightness write has proved the DSI path.

Every packet goes through one DSI DMA helper: the first version mixed the
embedded TPG shorts with the DMA long writes and the second page write never
completed (`long 6 bytes ... done 0`, `wedged dsi`), leaving the panel frozen
on its last frame. The stop-on-failure keeps a bad packet from costing the
next one's timeout too.

A 120 glass is proven by `intf ... fc` moving +120 a second and `panel`
near 120/120 while the UI moves; if only `present` doubles, the panel did
not take the new timing.

